---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE, hasContact } from '../site';
---

<Legal
  title="Contact"
  description="How to reach PetPomo about bugs, feature requests, privacy questions or a lost sync code."
  updated="2026-08-16"
  intro="Bugs, ideas, privacy questions, or a save you want deleted — all welcome."
>
  {
    hasContact ? (
      <>
        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          It is one person reading these, so a reply may take a few days. Please include what browser you are on if
          you are reporting a bug.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      /* Rendering a fake address would be worse than admitting there is not
         one yet: it bounces silently and it misleads anyone relying on it. */
      <>
        <h2>Not set up yet</h2>
        <p>
          PetPomo does not have a public contact address yet. It is a personal project that has only just gone live,
          and setting up an inbox that is actually monitored is on the list before anything here is monetised.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have found a bug or a privacy concern in the meantime, the most reliable route is to raise it
          wherever you found the link to this site.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2>What to include</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bugs</strong> — what you did, what happened, what you expected, and your browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy</strong> — see the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> first; it probably answers it.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Deleting a synced save</strong> — send the sync code and it will be removed. We cannot check who owns a
      code, so please only send your own.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Copyright</strong> — see the <a href="/copyright">copyright notice</a> for the takedown route.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What not to send</h2>
  <p>
    Please do not send passwords, payment details or anything sensitive. PetPomo has no accounts and takes no
    payments, so there is never a reason to.
  </p>
</Legal>
